{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") for TelemetryDeck in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app ID and your organization’s namespace, then posts to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/nom.telemetrydeck.com\/v3\/<namespace>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Each batch is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"split to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": 100 signals a request, as TelemetryDeck’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftSDK sends them; 333,333 bytes a signal, a third of Ingest API v3’s limit of 1,000,000; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1,000,000 bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, as TelemetryDeck documents none. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx (TelemetryDeck answers 503 while its queue","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is full), 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out, so import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID only says which app a signal belongs to, and TelemetryDeck’s own SDKs ship it inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every app, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to TelemetryDeck directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import TelemetryDeckEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let telemetryDeck = try HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ from the app's settings in the TelemetryDeck dashboard","    namespace: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your organization's namespace","    testMode: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose signals only Test Mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: telemetryDeck)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for an app ID that is empty or only whitespace,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and for a namespace TelemetryDeck doesn’t take. A namespace holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and can’t be "},{"code":"w","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"..","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"text":" has no default. TelemetryDeck shows test signals only in its Test Mode, apart from your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real users, and its SDK picks test mode for debug builds. Pass whatever your app uses to tell its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds apart, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if DEBUG"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" otherwise.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"User counts are sessions","anchor":"User-counts-are-sessions","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck counts users by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":". The destination sends the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":", hashed the way TelemetryDeck’s SDKs hash a user identifier:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SHA-256 of the lowercase UUID, in lowercase hex, with the SDKs’ default, empty salt."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck salts and hashes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" again on its server. The same session is also the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":", in the clear, so a salt of the app’s own would hide nothing, and the destination takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account, and no trace context."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So TelemetryDeck’s user counts are session counts. A person who opens the app three times is three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users, and its retention charts show how long a session lasts, not whether people come back. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the library’s default, for privacy. To count devices instead, put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"VendorIdentifierKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the records’ context and send them through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination that reads it, or write your own enricher and encoder that send the identifier you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose. This encoder sends the session alone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record with no session, from a tracker without the sessions enricher, is its own user: its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hash of the record’s identifier, and it has no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":". A record a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch keeps its session, and with it the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":" of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first send. Making up a session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would join unrelated records, and skipping the record would lose it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What TelemetryDeck receives","anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-receives","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a JSON array of signals, one per record. Every signal has:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as given, without surrounding whitespace;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s name;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"},{"type":"text","text":", the hashed session, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionID"},{"type":"text","text":", the session;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receivedAt"},{"text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so a signal sent late still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counts at the time it was tracked;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isTestMode"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"true\""},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"false\""},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.SDK.name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made with, and sit beside these, each keeping its JSON type. TelemetryDeck doesn’t index nested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart"},{"type":"text","text":" holding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"type":"text","text":", and the first element of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" property is left out. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floatValue"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, when the record has it, becomes TelemetryDeck’s built-in parameters:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Context"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameters"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".buildNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":".versionAndBuildNumber","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.modelName"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.operatingSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".systemVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".systemMajorVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":".systemMajorMinorVersion","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.RunContext.locale"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".language"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.UserPreference.region"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle identifier, the form factor and the network aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name or parameter name, once flattened, holds anything but ASCII letters, digits,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or is empty. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for one such name.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name or parameter name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck."},{"type":"text","text":", in any case: TelemetryDeck"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reserves that scope for its SDKs’ parameters and its server’s;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a parameter named as one of a signal’s own members, ","type":"text"},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"receivedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"isTestMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"floatValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", spelled exactly so: in the flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signal it would replace the member. A name like one in another case, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999, which TelemetryDeck can’t parse;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 333,333 bytes. TelemetryDeck refuses the whole request for a signal over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the encoder’s; a third leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What TelemetryDeck doesn’t report","anchor":"What-TelemetryDeck-doesnt-report","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck answers 200 to any namespace and any app ID it can read, so a typo in either loses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every signal without an error. Check that the first signals show up in the dashboard, in Test Mode","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when ","type":"text"},{"code":"testMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after TelemetryDeck stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and TelemetryDeck counts each copy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what TelemetryDeck receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to TelemetryDeck as signals, through its Ingest API v3.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-TelemetryDeck","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckSetupError"],"title":"Sending to TelemetryDeck"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"title":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework"},"references":{"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck’s limits on one request: 100 events and 1,000,000 bytes of body, and 333,333","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes of one event.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder\/batchlimit","kind":"symbol","title":"batchLimit"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","title":"BatchEncoder"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of TelemetryDeck’s Ingest API v3, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to an organization’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/v3\/<namespace>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder","title":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckEncodingError":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeckEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TelemetryDeckEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckencodingerror","title":"TelemetryDeckEncodingError"},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder/init(appID:testMode:plan:limit:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"init(appID:testMode:plan:limit:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/init(appID:testMode:plan:limit:)","abstract":[{"text":"An encoder of the events ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" describes, for the TelemetryDeck app ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", marking every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event as a test event or not as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"testMode"},{"text":" says,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and splitting each batch to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limit"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder\/init(appid:testmode:plan:limit:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"appID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"testMode","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentif